cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this software, or the pixel-purity method it implements, is useful in your
  work, an acknowledgement is appreciated. Please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "Reading a Drought from Space: PSF-weighted grassland condition and cut detection from Sentinel-2"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end remote-sensing pipeline for the 2026 Swiss drought. It builds a
  point-spread-function-weighted pixel purity mask over a persistence-filtered
  master parcel set, derives season vegetation-index trajectories and anomalies
  per management regime, and detects grassland cutting events from Sentinel-2
  time series with a scored detector. The repository runs end to end on
  synthetic data calibrated to the real distributions, so no restricted input
  data is required to reproduce the pipeline.
authors:
